<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aeolis</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Aeolia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aeolis was the ancient name of the north-western coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> and the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a>, settled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeolians">Aeolian Greeks</a> from the 11th century BCE. Its cities, including Cyme, Myrina and those of Lesbos, formed a league and spoke the Aeolic dialect of Greek. They came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a>, then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, and later formed part of the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aeolis.jpg" alt="Aeolis" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Georges Jansoone JoJan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Izmir016.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
